# ---------------------------------------------------------------- papers
# The corpus is 402 MB of PUBLISHER PDFs. Do not commit them:
#   · redistributing paywalled papers is copyright infringement, private repo or not
#   · they are hard links to a central corpus, so git would store full copies
#   · GitHub warns above 50 MB per file
#
# Rebuild your own copy instead — see README, "Getting the papers".
resources/papers/**/*.pdf
resources/papers/**/*.PDF
resources/papers/**/*_suppl*
resources/papers/**/*supplement*

# Cloned tool repos (symlinks into the corpus; clone them yourself)
resources/papers/**/[A-Za-z]*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- books
# Coop is CC-BY 3.0 and Harmon is freely published, so both are legally
# redistributable — but they are 96 MB and 12 MB. Fetch with scripts/get_books.sh.
resources/books/**/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- research logs
# Codex JSONL transcripts: large, machine-only, and regenerable.
# research/briefs/ and research/raw/ ARE committed — they are the audit trail.
research/logs/
research/*.log
research/download_log.jsonl*
research/dl_run.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- junk
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
scratchpad/

# stray driver output (1.2 MB, regenerable)
research/download.out
research/chain.out
research/*.out
research/refs.json.bak

# audit trail kept locally, not published
research/

# local tooling, not published
scripts/
